21	URG-INF-001	URGENCIAS_BANDERAS_ROJAS	Harrison Principios de Medicina Interna / Surviving Sepsis Campaign 2021 / Farreras-Rozman Medicina Interna	Fiebre > 38,5 °C con qSOFA ≥ 2, petequias, inmunosupresión o neutropenia: urgencia; en dengue evitar AINE y aspirina.\n\nLa fiebre mayor de 38,5 °C requiere buscar el foco y evaluar signos de gravedad. Aplicar qSOFA: frecuencia respiratoria de 22 o más, alteración del estado mental y presión sistólica de 100 mmHg o menos; dos o más puntos sugieren sepsis y exigen manejo urgente (hemocultivos, lactato, antibiótico y fluidos en la primera hora). Otras banderas rojas: rigidez de nuca, exantema petequial, dolor abdominal intenso, disuria con dolor lumbar, inmunosupresión, neutropenia (fiebre de 38,3 °C o más, o de 38 °C sostenida durante una hora, con neutrófilos menores de 500/µL), esplenectomía, posoperatorio, quimioterapia, VIH, soplo nuevo (endocarditis) y viaje a zonas endémicas (malaria, dengue). En dengue, el dolor abdominal, el vómito persistente, el sangrado de mucosas, el letargo y el hematocrito en ascenso son signos de alarma; usar paracetamol y evitar AINE y aspirina por riesgo hemorrágico. Los ancianos pueden no presentar fiebre. Fiebre con ictericia y dolor en hipocondrio derecho sugiere colangitis. Una temperatura mayor de 41 °C es una emergencia.	[0.068886,0.137772,0.025832,0.043054,0.275545,0.060275,0.22388,0.025832,0.137772,0.154994,0.094719,0.068886,0.241102,0.172216,0.068886,0.146383,0.129162,0.129162,0.103329,0.120551,0.068886,0.051665,0.077497,0.051665,0.051665,0.068886,0.060275,0.094719,0.068886,0.154994,0.103329,0.215269,0.043054,0.068886,0.146383,0.163605,0.077497,0.043054,0.129162,0.154994,0.146383,0.094719,0.180826,0.094719,0.129162,0.215269,0.206659,0.146383,0.094719,0.025832,0.120551,0.11194,0.043054,0.086108,0.086108,0.060275,0.137772,0.11194,0.198048,0.025832,0.120551,0.163605,0.086108,0.11194]
22	URG-ABD-001	URGENCIAS_BANDERAS_ROJAS	Argente Semiología Médica / Harrison Principios de Medicina Interna / Farreras-Rozman Medicina Interna	Dolor abdominal con rigidez, rebote, hipotensión o dolor desproporcionado: urgencia quirúrgica; en mujer fértil, beta-hCG obligatoria.\n\nAbdomen agudo: dolor abdominal de inicio reciente que puede requerir cirugía. Banderas rojas: rigidez o defensa abdominal involuntaria, signo de rebote, dolor que precede al vómito, distensión con ausencia de ventosidad, hipotensión, taquicardia, fiebre, sangrado digestivo, ictericia y dolor desproporcionado respecto al examen (isquemia mesentérica). Diagnósticos a excluir: apendicitis, colecistitis y colangitis, pancreatitis (investigar triglicéridos y alcohol), obstrucción intestinal, perforación, diverticulitis, aneurisma aórtico roto (mayores de 60 años con dolor abdominal o lumbar y shock), embarazo ectópico (mujer en edad fértil: beta-hCG obligatoria), torsión testicular, cetoacidosis diabética y causas torácicas (infarto inferior, neumonía basal). Ancianos, diabéticos e inmunosuprimidos presentan signos atenuados. El examen físico seriado es más útil que una sola evaluación, y la analgesia no debe retrasar el estudio. Evitar AINE si se sospecha sangrado o lesión renal. Dolor abdominal con náusea y respiración rápida en un paciente con SGLT2i o dieta cetogénica obliga a medir cetonas.	[0.173821,0.191203,0.112984,0.191203,0.199894,0.060837,0.104293,0.043455,0.112984,0.112984,0.156439,0.199894,0.043455,0.069528,0.086911,0.043455,0.052146,0.069528,0.017382,0.156439,0.078219,0.104293,0.034764,0.104293,0.095602,0.095602,0.112984,0.112984,0.052146,0.043455,0.112984,0.191203,0.086911,0.095602,0.139057,0.139057,0.225967,0.095602,0.017382,0.112984,0.069528,0.156439,0.217276,0.130366,0.182512,0.026073,0.121675,0.278114,0.095602,0.060837,0.052146,0.112984,0.139057,0.069528,0.086911,0.069528,0.112984,0.173821,0.104293,0.043455,0.199894,0.060837,0.078219,0.208585]
23	FAR-ALE-001	FARMACOLOGIA_ALERGIAS	Goodman & Gilman Bases Farmacológicas de la Terapéutica / Harrison Principios de Medicina Interna	Alergia a un AINE: determinar si es cruzada (COX-1) o selectiva; el metamizol puede reaccionar de forma cruzada y causar agranulocitosis.\n\nAntes de indicar un AINE, hacer cross-check de alergia: se distinguen reacciones cruzadas (por inhibición de COX-1, con urticaria, angioedema o enfermedad respiratoria exacerbada por AINE con asma y pólipos nasales; reaccionan aspirina, ibuprofeno, naproxeno, diclofenaco y ketorolaco) y reacciones selectivas a un solo fármaco. En hipersensibilidad cruzada se evitan todos los inhibidores de COX-1; el paracetamol en dosis de hasta 500 mg suele tolerarse y los inhibidores selectivos de COX-2 (celecoxib, etoricoxib) pueden usarse bajo supervisión alergológica. El metamizol (dipirona), de uso frecuente en Latinoamérica, puede reaccionar de forma cruzada y además causa agranulocitosis. Contraindicaciones no alérgicas: úlcera o sangrado digestivo, enfermedad renal crónica, insuficiencia cardiaca, cirrosis con ascitis, tercer trimestre del embarazo, anticoagulantes y la combinación de AINE con IECA o ARA II y diurético (riesgo de lesión renal aguda), sobre todo con deshidratación. El antecedente de anafilaxia, síndrome de Stevens-Johnson o necrólisis epidérmica tóxica por un AINE contraindica el grupo hasta una evaluación especializada.	[0.141632,0.099976,0.116638,0.06665,0.283264,0.158295,0.141632,0.06665,0.133301,0.083313,0.116638,0.116638,0.216614,0.091644,0.041657,0.024994,0.06665,0.083313,0.099976,0.024994,0.12497,0.158295,0.141632,0.108307,0.116638,0.049988,0.083313,0.108307,0.12497,0.099976,0.141632,0.099976,0.074982,0.158295,0.133301,0.06665,0.099976,0.141632,0.216614,0.174957,0.183289,0.091644,0.108307,0.116638,0.249939,0.058319,0.108307,0.174957,0.149964,0.091644,0.133301,0.158295,0.116638,0.058319,0.099976,0.041657,0.099976,0.12497,0.083313,0.141632,0.024994,0.074982,0.166626,0.049988]
24	FAR-ALE-002	FARMACOLOGIA_ALERGIAS	Goodman & Gilman Bases Farmacológicas de la Terapéutica / Harrison Principios de Medicina Interna	Alergia referida a penicilina: caracterizar la reacción; nunca reexponer ante SJS/TEN o DRESS; la reactividad cruzada con cefalosporinas es baja y depende de cadenas laterales.\n\nCerca del 10 % de los pacientes refiere alergia a penicilina, pero menos del 10 % de ellos (alrededor del 1 % de la población) tiene una alergia mediada por IgE verdadera; el resto tolera el fármaco tras evaluación. Interrogar tipo, tiempo y gravedad: urticaria, angioedema, anafilaxia o hipotensión en la primera hora indican reacción inmediata; un exantema tardío benigno, sin ampollas ni compromiso sistémico, tiene bajo riesgo. La regla PEN-FAST ayuda a estratificar. Nunca reexponer ante antecedente de síndrome de Stevens-Johnson, necrólisis epidérmica tóxica, DRESS, nefritis intersticial o anemia hemolítica por penicilina. La reactividad cruzada con cefalosporinas es de 1 a 2 % y depende de cadenas laterales similares: amoxicilina y ampicilina las comparten con cefalexina, cefadroxilo y cefaclor, mientras que ceftriaxona y cefazolina tienen cadenas distintas y suelen ser seguras salvo reacción grave. Con carbapenémicos la reactividad es menor de 1 %. El exantema por amoxicilina durante una mononucleosis no equivale a alergia. Documentar la reacción y derivar para prueba cutánea o provocación oral supervisada.	[0.200721,0.064231,0.20875,0.120432,0.216778,0.176634,0.088317,0.104375,0.192692,0.120432,0.056202,0.024086,0.024086,0.13649,0.024086,0.128461,0.088317,0.056202,0.200721,0.088317,0.120432,0.064231,0.144519,0.152548,0.192692,0.120432,0.048173,0.096346,0.080288,0.112404,0.112404,0.112404,0.040144,0.248894,0.168605,0.064231,0.216778,0.128461,0.072259,0.120432,0.152548,0.024086,0.120432,0.048173,0.080288,0.096346,0.144519,0.064231,0.144519,0.152548,0.13649,0.13649,0.056202,0.120432,0.160577,0.112404,0.040144,0.168605,0.152548,0.096346,0.056202,0.032115,0.072259,0.096346]
25	FAR-ALE-003	FARMACOLOGIA_ALERGIAS	Goodman & Gilman Bases Farmacológicas de la Terapéutica / Harrison Principios de Medicina Interna	Alergia a sulfas: aclarar si fue antibiótico o no antibiótico; la reactividad cruzada entre grupos no está respaldada, salvo antecedente de SJS/TEN o DRESS.\n\nEl término alergia a sulfas es ambiguo. Las sulfonamidas antibacterianas (trimetoprima-sulfametoxazol, sulfadiazina) poseen un grupo arilamina en N4 y un anillo heterocíclico en N1, asociados a hipersensibilidad. Las sulfonamidas no antibióticas (furosemida, tiazidas, sulfonilureas, acetazolamida, celecoxib, sumatriptán) carecen de ellos, y la reactividad cruzada con los antibióticos no está respaldada; el riesgo parece reflejar una predisposición alérgica general. Aun así, ante antecedente de síndrome de Stevens-Johnson, necrólisis epidérmica tóxica o DRESS por cualquier sulfonamida, evitar todo el grupo hasta una evaluación especializada. Aclarar la reacción: exantema, fiebre, citopenias, hepatitis o lesión de mucosas. Las sulfas no se relacionan con sulfitos, sulfatos, contraste yodado ni mariscos. El trimetoprima-sulfametoxazol requiere cross-check por hiperpotasemia con IECA, ARA II o espironolactona, aumento de creatinina, hipoglucemia con sulfonilureas, potenciación de warfarina y déficit de G6PD. En pacientes con dieta baja en carbohidratos y diuréticos, vigilar potasio y sodio al usarlo.	[0.07312,0.048747,0.154364,0.081244,0.308729,0.105618,0.178738,0.129991,0.227484,0.105618,0.089369,0.07312,0.056871,0.064996,0.07312,0.089369,0,0.121867,0.121867,0.016249,0.105618,0.040622,0.14624,0.105618,0.064996,0.024373,0.129991,0.251858,0.121867,0.129991,0.07312,0.07312,0.14624,0.243733,0.194987,0.040622,0.056871,0.170613,0.097493,0.154364,0.07312,0.089369,0.154364,0.105618,0.14624,0.105618,0.178738,0.064996,0.113742,0.024373,0.024373,0.081244,0.024373,0.138116,0.121867,0.024373,0.113742,0.097493,0.081244,0.268107,0.089369,0.07312,0.064996,0.170613]
